<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vitória, Espírito Santo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vitória is the capital of the Brazilian state of Espírito Santo, built mainly on an island in a bay on the Atlantic coast. It was founded in 1551, when settlers moved there from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vila-velha">Vila Velha</a> for safety from indigenous attacks, and became the captaincy's capital. Today it is a major port, especially for the export of iron ore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vitoria-espirito-santo.jpg" alt="Vitória, Espírito Santo" width="320" height="130" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Romerito Pontes from São Carlos · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:-2016-11-05_ao_13-_Vit%C3%B3ria_94_Romerito_Pontes_(30875449812)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
